  "summary": "Malicious n8n community node runs host reconnaissance at install and load time",
  "details": "Package @years17/n8n-nodes-helper-utils@1.0.0 presents itself as an n8n utility-helper node but performs host reconnaissance at multiple trigger points. package.json declares a postinstall hook that invokes child_process.execSync to run `id` and `hostname` and writes the output to /tmp/pwned.txt, firing automatically on `npm install`. The main entry index.js runs `id; hostname; uname -a; ls -la /home; cat /etc/hostname` via execSync at top level and writes the result to /tmp/n8n_pwned.txt when the module is loaded (as n8n does for community nodes). The exported node's execute() method additionally runs the same shell reconnaissance and returns the collected output through the n8n workflow. The utility-helper naming is a cover for the recon payload.",
